Z||000000||chicagoGT||09-03-2000||06:28 PM||||have an opprotunity to purchase a 85 gt for parts. i intend to do an archie swap in my 86gt and need to know if i can basically do all the work on the 85 cradle as well as do the test fitting in the 85 car and then use the whole asembly in the 86.||||reg||5
Z||000001||V8Fiero||09-03-2000||09:25 PM||||You should be able to do everything but the test fitting. If it was me doing it in different cars, I would just mount the engine/trans assembly on the 85 cradle (just bolt down the front engine mount). Remember you have to cut the hole in the fender well for the water pump drive system. Wouldnt make much sense doing this in the 85 since its not staying there. Dont weld the front engine mount until you trial fit in the 86. I also used the archie kit.<P>Good luck.<BR>Scooter||||reg||6
